    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **255 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `displayName` feature for owner creation so the API returns the owner's name formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema. This makes the OpenAPI code generator produce a `displayName` field on the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` with an expression that computes `displayName` from the stored names when mapping an `Owner` to an `OwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nBecause the controller's `addOwner`/`getOwner` both go through `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(...)`, the computed `displayName` is returned everywhere an owner is serialized, satisfying the acceptance test (`$.displayName` = `\"<LastName>, John\"`) and leaving all pre-existing tests passing.",
